          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a document refers to the J45 family, is that a code or a category?",
          "answer": "The J45 family refers to a category, not a specific code. In the ICD-10-CM (International Classification of Diseases, 10th Revision, Clinical Modification), J45 is the category for asthma and is part of Chapter 10, which covers diseases of the respiratory system. \n\nThis category does not stand alone as a three-character code. Instead, it is used in combination with additional characters to specify severity and state of the disease. Each combination of these characteristics creates distinct codes for different types and presentations of asthma. This information can be found in the document titled \"Coding asthma: J45 and its severity and exacerbation axes.\"\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
